meta {
  name: Firebase Login (Google)
  type: http
  seq: 3
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/student/auth/firebase
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "id_token": "{{studentFirebaseIdToken}}",
    "fcm_token": "{{studentFcmToken}}"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status === 200) {
    const data = res.getBody();
    if (data.data) {
      if (data.data.accessToken) {
        bru.setEnvVar("accessToken", data.data.accessToken);
      }
      if (data.data.refreshToken) {
        bru.setEnvVar("studentRefreshToken", data.data.refreshToken);
      }
      if (data.data.user && data.data.user.id) {
        bru.setEnvVar("studentId", data.data.user.id);
      }
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Sign in a student using a Firebase Google ID token obtained from the Flutter app.

  FLOW:
  1. Flutter calls Firebase Google Sign-In → gets an ID token
  2. Send that ID token here → backend verifies it with Firebase Admin SDK
  3. Backend upserts the student in Postgres and issues its own JWT
  4. Use the returned accessToken for all subsequent student requests

  FIRST LOGIN: creates a new student record (source: "google")
  RETURNING LOGIN: updates name and avatar, issues a fresh token pair

  ACCOUNT LINKING: if a student previously signed up via phone OTP using the
  same email address, their existing account is linked to the Google ID —
  all their data (applications, etc.) is preserved.

  Set {{studentFirebaseIdToken}} to the ID token from the Flutter Firebase SDK.
  Leave {{studentFcmToken}} empty if not testing push notifications.

  Response:
  - accessToken: JWT (15 min), auto-captured into {{accessToken}}
  - refreshToken: long-lived token (90 days), also set as httpOnly cookie,
                  auto-captured into {{studentRefreshToken}}
  - user: { id, fullName, email, avatarUrl }
  - studentId auto-captured into {{studentId}}
}
